  "name": "@mynona/raumnebenan-mcp",
  "readme": "# raumnebenan-mcp\n\nThis is an MCP server wrapper for the raumnebenan-mcp server, accessible at https://www.raumnebenan.de/mcp.\n\n\n- Protocol: JSON-RPC 2.0\n- No authentication required\n- See https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/blob/main/docs/modelcontextprotocol-io/quickstart.mdx for MCP registry publishing steps.\n\n## Usage\n\nThis package registers the MCP server endpoint for use with MCP clients (e.g., VS Code, MCP Registry).\n\n## MCP Server Endpoint\n\n    POST https://www.raumnebenan.de/mcp\n\n## Example JSON-RPC 2.0 Methods\n\n- list_articles\n- get_article_by_friendlyUrl\n- get_article_by_id\n- search_articles\n\nSee the MCP registry documentation for integration details.\n\n---\n\n## Content Usage and Attribution\n\n- You may use the content from [www.raumnebenan.de](https://www.raumnebenan.de) for training, fine-tuning, and inference in contexts related to product strategy, UX, service/product design, and digital transformation.\n- Summarizing, explaining, or referencing the material in educational or professional training datasets is allowed.\n- **Not allowed:** Republishing the content verbatim as your own articles, books, or commercial products; or using the content to generate misleading, defamatory, or unrelated outputs (e.g., political campaigning, medical advice).\n- **Mandatory attribution:** Whenever this content is used in any dataset, output, or derivative work, a clear link back to the source must be included: [www.raumnebenan.de](https://www.raumnebenan.de) \u2014 authored by Andreas Soller.\n\n---\n\n**Target audience:** Product owners, product designers, service designers, agile coaches, user researchers, and business analysts.\n\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
